    "body": "Backports:\n* #35168\n\n`v31.1` still has the pre-fix `LoadBlockIndex`. It re-adds a pruned block to `m_blocks_unlinked` when its parent is header-only (#35050). When the next block connects, `CheckBlockIndex` fails with `Assertion failed: (!foundInUnlinked)`. `-checkblockindex` is on by default only on regtest, so this crashes functional-test suites run against 31.x. With default settings, nodes on mainnet, testnet and signet do not run this check, so they do not crash.\n\nBoth commits are clean cherry-picks (`-x`). The only difference from master is context in `test_runner.py`. The new `feature_prune_stale_fork.py` fails on the `v31.1` release binary with the assertion above. It passes on this branch, built from `depends`. Two runs each, on macOS arm64.\n\n*Made with my usual tools: a computer, the Internet and an LLM. The mistakes, as usual, are all mine.*\n\n",
